Security group to be created
9. Provision Infrastructure

Run:

terraform apply

Type:

yes

Press Enter.

Terraform creates:

EC2 instance
Security group
10. Verify EC2 Instance on AWS
Open EC2 Console

Search:

EC2
Open
Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud
Verify Instance
Left sidebar → Instances

You should see:

Terraform-EC2

Status:

Running
11. Connect to EC2 using SSH
Create Key Pair (If Needed)

In AWS Console:

EC2 → Key Pairs
Create key pair
Download .pem file
Attach Key Pair in Terraform (Optional)

Add inside aws_instance block:

key_name = "my-key"

Run again:

terraform apply
12. Connect Using SSH
Get Public IP

Open EC2 instance and copy:

Public IPv4 address
SSH Command (Linux/macOS)

Run:

ssh -i my-key.pem ec2-user@<Public-IP>

Example:

ssh -i my-key.pem ec2-user@13.233.xxx.xxx
Validate Deployment

After login run:

hostname

Instance accessible successfully.

13. Destroy Infrastructure

To terminate all created resources run:

terraform destroy

Type:

yes

Terraform deletes:

EC2 instance
Security group
